foreign  [Music]  to our new original this week we talk  about a film that is right at the top of  many fans wish lists The Amazing  Spider-Man 3 the sequel that should have  completed the trilogy starring Andrew  Garfield the reality is well known  because so far there are only two movies  with Garfield Spider-Man and for the  time being he was superseded by Tom  Holland for the MCU yet today we want to  ask ourselves what a lead sequel to the  film series could look like and why  another part may not be so unlikely in  the future enjoy  if we look at the two predecessors we  can derive a certain direction for The  Amazing Spider-Man 3. the first The  Amazing Spider-Man movie with Andrew  Garfield was released in 2012 something  that immediately stands out especially  in the year 2022 is that the film's  title alone sets it apart from the other  two film series starring Toby Maguire  and Tom Holland Garfield Spider-Man is  thus obviously based more on the comic  book with the same title which has been  published since 1963 and is by far the  most widely distributed comic book from  the Spider-Man universe from its  establishment in 1963 to the 700th issue  in 2012 the comic book was consistently  published and is accordingly extensive  the other two franchises are also based  more or less on these Comics but those  responsible always use the original in a  slightly different way and at times  Incorporated a great deal of artistic  freedom however the comic book original  is not the reason that the Amazing  Spider-Man 3 is once again a big Topic  at least among fans the hype surrounding  Garfield undoubtedly stems from the  release of Spider-Man no way home about  a year ago when many were taken back to  the old days by the universe spanning  reunion of the three Peter Parkers but  back to the beginnings of The Amazing  Spider-Man the first of two parts was  released in 2012 and thus exactly five  years after the trilogy with Toby  Maguire and five years before the  trilogy with Tom Holland Peter Parker is  initially a typical teenager who lost  his parents at an early age and is  living with Uncle Ben and Aunt May his  father was a renowned genetic researcher  and a left behind briefcase eventually  leads Peter to former business associate  Dr Kurt Connors who was researching  cross-species genetics at Oscorp  Industries as a supposed intern there  Peter is bitten by a radioactive spider  giving him his superpowers he seeks out  Connors and ends up working with him as  in the film series with Tobey Maguire  here too Uncle Ben is shot by a robber  after an argument with Peter this  triggers great feelings of guilt in the  young Peter and results in him becoming  a masked superhero to make the streets  of New York City a little safer in  addition there is of course again a  crush on the main character who here is  not called Mary Jane or MJ but Gwen  Stacy over the course of the story Dr  Kurt Connors turns out to be a villain  who after self-testing a regeneration  serum transforms into a superhumanly  fast and strong lizard the so-called  lizard then intends to subject the  city's inhabitants to the same fate but  has stopped at the last minute by  Spider-Man tragically Gwen's father  George dies in the process and in his  last minutes begs Peter to keep his  daughter out of trouble the second part  titled The Amazing Spider-Man 2 picks up  directly where the previous part ended  and First shows the turbulent superhero  existence in the urban Canyons of New  York City at first more clarity is  brought to the mysterious death of  Peter's parents and later we get to see  him and Gwen trying to reconcile their  love lives with his existence as a  superhero things also go their way at  Oscorp Gwen has the chance to intern  there and Peter saves the life of  company electrician Max Dillon moreover  company president Norman Osborne dies of  a strange disease that has also spread  to his son in the meantime the rescued  electrician from the beginning of the  film has fallen into a tank of electric  eels and us has been involuntarily given  superpowers after he's captured by  Spider-Man and admitted to the infamous  ravencroft Institute he begins to  develop a strong hatred for Spider-Man  Harry Osborne meanwhile sees the Oscorp  spider's venom as the last resort to  cure his terminal illness Peter however  refuses to donate blood because of  unclear implications which leads Harry  in desperation to release Electro and  with his help obtain the Spider Venom on  oscorp's premises this transforms him  into the Green Goblin and a final  showdown ensues between the former best  friends unfortunately Gwen Falls victim  to the final fight which in turn Peter  does not cope well with giving up his  superhero existence for a while he does  however return to fight the villain  Rhino recruited by Harry with the  outcome still being unclear  now that we've refreshed our memories of  the two The Amazing Spider-Man films  let's turn our attention to the  potential plot especially because of the  open ending of part two there are enough  options to follow up with a third movie  that it is technically and legally  possible to bring back Andrew Garfield  is something we have known since no way  home at the latest a parallel universe  alongside the one with Tom Holland is  also conceivable outside the MCU and as  before at Sony Pictures there is one  drawback however by the time the Amazing  Spider-Man 3 is released Garfield will  be at least 10 years older than before  and well into his 40s so there won't be  much left of the youthful Spidey  Aesthetics by then it would therefore  not make any sense for the new film to  immediately pick up where the  predecessor left off unless the final  battle against rhino had taken such a  toll on him that he had aged many years  in the meantime so the plans for a  sequel that were made back then are  rather useless that's why we're now  looking to a few hints about a possible  alternative storyline based on various  sources as early as 2015 George Stacy  actor Dennis Leary talked about the  proposed plot in an IGN interview  according to the interview he himself  would have played a role in the third  part in spite of his death on screen the  idea circulated that Spidey could revive  his deceased companions through a  mysterious magic formula with which he  could bring back George his girlfriend  Gwen and presumably also his Uncle Ben  indeed this idea sounds completely  absurd and would probably have been  dismissed as complete nonsense if not  for the statement of an actor involved  however there is actually at least some  justification for it in the comics  through Professor Miles Warren AKA  Jackal various Spidey clones were  created from Peter's DNA in the original  the same could be done with Gwen and  other deceased characters this story arc  already divided the fan base when the  comic was released as it almost makes  things too easy and takes away the  impact and significance of the previous  deaths in 2017 director Mark Webb also  spoke about the planned plot two years  after the Amazing Spider-Man franchise  was signed off according to his  statements he also deceased Norman  Osborne who was embodied by Chris Cooper  at the time would have returned in a  significantly larger role than before in  the third part he would have taken over  the the role of the Green Goblin from  his son after he came back from the dead  the main villain would have been Gustav  Fierce aka the gentleman who had no  direct superpowers but can make up for  it with his wealth and tricks later he  would have led the Sinister Six in the  spin-offs finally we would like to  mention the role of Emma Stone as Gwen  Stacy Not only would she have returned  as Peter's girlfriend but later she  would have taken on the role as the  villain carnage this would have adapted  storylines from the Ultimate Comics and  certainly created an exciting  constellation Garfield himself also  commented in The Amazing Spider-Man from  time to time during the years sometimes  he denied further participation due to  his age other times he expressed his  wishes for a hypothetical The Amazing  Spider-Man 3. among these is a clash  between Spidey and Eddie Brock AKA Venom  as he confirmed in the happy sad  confused podcast earlier this year  additionally there was already fan art  showing him in a symbiote costume that  would certainly come in handy when  fighting Venom much like in Spider-Man 3  with Tobey Maguire at a cost of course  in summary there are various ideas about  the storyline that don't stem from the  image nation of the fans but rather from  the statements of the people involved  and the comics  let's take a brief look at the  production background of The Amazing  Spider-Man 3. basically Sony didn't want  to leave it at a pure Trilogy around the  friendly neighborhood spider but instead  wanted to initiate an extensive  franchise in 2013 the third film was  announced with a theatrical release in  2016 and two years later the fourth part  of the main series was supposed to kick  off in addition two spin-offs were  planned for the Sinister Six as well as  Venom and Carnage the directors Drew  Goddard and Alex kurtzman were also  already confirmed the spin-offs were to  be released in parallel to the main  series the plans for the Saudi franchise  outside the MCU were therefore quite  ambitious and the reflections were well  Advanced to Sony's utter astonishment  however The Amazing Spider-Man 2  performed poorly at the box office and  generally received mixed reviews as a  result screenwriter Roberto orsi a  pivotal member of the team left the  pre-production team to work on Star Trek  Beyond thus the situation was  unfavorable and the movie was pushed  back further in November 2014 the hacker  group Guardians Of Peace infiltrated  Sony pictures and leaked a large number  of internal documents alongside various  emails between high-ranking employees  these also included details about the  Amazing Spider-Man it was revealed for  example that Emma Stone was in talks to  return in The Amazing Spider-Man 3 after  which her character Gwen would have been  resurrected in addition further films by  Sam Raimi were planned and even initial  ideas for a future Crossover with Andrew  Garfield and Toby Maguire were being  discussed however the subsequent  negotiations between Sony and Marvel  over future film rights did not go in  favor of The Amazing Spider-Man and  ultimately put an end to the  far-reaching dreams of those responsible  instead in 2015 both parties concluded a  deal that Spider-Man would move to the  Marvel Cinematic Universe in the future  which effectively put an end to the  Amazing Spider-Man as the Sony franchise  ironically the renewed hype around Sony  Spider-Man was created by Marvel's  Spider-Man no way home at the end of  2021 and the speculations took off we  still don't know whether the Amazing  Spider-Man 3 will ever be released there  are several conflicting statements  circulated however one should not forget  that Garfield denied his involvement in  the film in the run-up to Spider-Man no  way home more or less credibly and we  all know what the end result was so we  shouldn't give up hope for another The  Amazing Spider-Man  we hope you enjoyed our new original  episode about a possible The Amazing  Spider-Man 3 and would appreciate it if  you shared the video with your friends  How likely do you think a continuation  of the film series with Andrew Garfield  is and which roles and storylines would  you most like to see feel free to tell  us in the comments  [Music]  thank you

